            "reasoning": "All three receiving recipes explicitly point to JCM915. Its modified Wolfe mineral stock starts with JCM151 trace minerals and changes final Na2MoO4·2H2O to0.4 g/L, CuSO4·5H2O to0.02 g/L and NiCl2·6H2O to0.01 g/L. This differs from JCM628, JCM265, and the existing MIM Modified Wolfes Minerals and EDTA-based ATCC/Wolfes records. JCM151 retains MnSO4·xH2O and AlK(SO4)2 as printed; unprovided hydration must not be supplied. Current exact proposal basis: JCM915 explicitly specifies FINAL0.4g/L Na2MoO4·2H2O,0.02g/L CuSO4·5H2O and0.01g/L NiCl2·6H2O: only these three retain G_PER_L. Other constituents and1L added-water amount retain the JCM151 source batch basis; their final concentrations are not independently specified. This mixed representation preserves the original instruction rather than fabricating a single final-volume recipe. KOH pH adjustment remains unquantified. The full named source preparation is scientifically identified. Raw local names and bare numbered pointers are preserved as REJECTED_LABEL, not global resolver aliases; each original occurrence receives only its explicit source-qualified assignment. Component grounding, variable titrant amounts and unrelated release assertions retain their stated boundaries.",
