            "reasoning": "NBRC943 explicitly defines Metal salt solution44 in its***footnote: Na-EDTA250mg,ZnSO4·7H2O1095mg,FeSO4·7H2O0.5g,MnSO4·H2O154mg,CuSO4·5H2O39.2mg,Co(NO3)2·6H2O24.8mg,Na2B4O7·10H2O17.7mg in100mL water plus a few drops concentratedH2SO4. Store dark/cold5C.50mL enters1L Modified Hutner solution. Existing Metall_Salt_Sol_44 and Metals_44_see_below lack formulation-bound provenance; lexical similarity cannot decide their identity with this stock. Completeness reassessment: NBRC943*** explicitly lists100mLwater plus a fewdropsconcentratedH2SO4. Official MICRO0000456 gives corresponding amountsper1Lwater, not100mL; current source-linked Metallsalt44 ingredient615occurrences referenceDSMZ590, whose admitted complete formulation isalso1L. This formulation has tenfold the precursor mass per stated added-water volume of those candidates. An exact ratio of final solution concentrations is not established because measured final volumes are not supplied. The source preparations are therefore not merged. Preserve Na-EDTA saltstoichiometry unspecified. A native-validated isolated owner proposal now records this operational stock with its complete source-listed preparation inputs. Both lane proposals transcribe the same NBRC943 Metal salt solution44 table. In named case116 it is a 50 mL nested component of Modified Hutner solution, not the whole Hutner preparation or an exact alias for it. Canonical stock identity is shared; the parent keeps its separate stock identity.",
