            "reasoning": "NBRC1321*******footnote defines1M sulfide stock as24g Na2S·9H2O in100mL water, filter sterilized and stored underN2; the recipe takes1.5mL. This supplies the nonahydrate and solvent omitted by the short label. It is neither neutralized sulfide nor5% nonahydrate stock. Completeness reassessment: Footnote*******states24gNa2S·9H2O and100mLdistilledwater,filtersterilizedandstoredunderN2; sourcecallsit1M. Preservewateraddedbasisandnominalmolaritywithoutasserting24gperfinal100mL. Receivingdoseis1.5mL; different5%andneutralizedsulfidestocksremainseparate. A native-validated isolated owner proposal now records this operational stock with its complete source-listed preparation inputs. NBRC1257 uses 12 g Na2S·9H2O plus 50 mL distilled water; NBRC1321 uses 24 g plus 100 mL. Both give the same precursor-to-added-water ratio, call the preparation 1.0 M, specify filtration and storage under N2. This is formulation equivalence at scaled batch size, not a claim that either is made up to a final volume. MIM #1167 successor removes the preparation/storage atmosphere gas from material components while retaining the actual gas condition in source evidence and notes. No gas-solute amount or final dissolved speciation is inferred.",
