            "reasoning": "NBRC1257 prints12g Na2S·9H2O plus50mL added distilled water; NBRC1321 prints24g plus100mL. Both call the preparation1M, specify filter sterilization and storage underN2. Proportional literal batches and identical handling support one canonical source-stock identity; no final volume or240g/L concentration is inferred. The NBRC1257 receiving dose is1.5mL. Frozen12G_PER_L loses the preparation basis and is not adopted. Current exact proposal basis: NBRC1257 uses 12 g Na2S·9H2O plus 50 mL distilled water; NBRC1321 uses 24 g plus 100 mL. Both give the same precursor-to-added-water ratio, call the preparation 1.0 M, specify filtration and storage under N2. This is formulation equivalence at scaled batch size, not a claim that either is made up to a final volume. The full named source preparation is scientifically identified. Raw local names and bare numbered pointers are preserved as REJECTED_LABEL, not global resolver aliases; each original occurrence receives only its explicit source-qualified assignment. Component grounding, variable titrant amounts and unrelated release assertions retain their stated boundaries.",
