            "disposition": "new_distinct_ingredient_proposal",
            "reasoning": "TOGO M578 and linked JCM574 define MDS salt water as a separate salt formulation and add 833 mL to the receiving preparation. The stock contains NaCl240 g, MgSO4·7H2O35 g, MgCl2·6H2O30 g, KCl7 g and 5 mL1 M CaCl2, brought to1 L and pH7.5 with1 M Tris base. This is not a generic salt or seawater identity. Frozen833 G_PER_L loses the source volume unit. JCM574 defines this complete seven-input stock and uses833mL in the receiving medium. The final stock pH is7.5; preparation is source-owned. Three solution/solvent parts retain raw supplied-form names without guessed component IDs. The whole stock has an established source identity; these part-grounding gaps do not make it an unresolved mixture identity. Context-only source labels are retained as non-resolving REJECTED_LABEL; RAW_TEXT source annotations alone do not enforce that scope.",
            "applicability": "Individually reviewed source case 4: 'MDS salt water (see below)'; all 1 original occurrence IDs and full frozen recipe contexts are retained in RS-004-FROZEN. Primary references are scoped to those exact recipes or explicitly identified chemical/product candidates; no identity or concentration is transferred to a different preparation. This review preserves every inherited source/native hold and does not approve roles or release.",
