            "reasoning": "The JCM11-derived TOGO M4 record specifies200mL filtered tomato juice atpH7.0, while the completed medium is adjusted topH6.0. These pH values describe different preparation stages. Current JCM11 returns Nothing found; primary confirmation of the original collection recipe remains unavailable. This qualified liquid material cannot be merged with untreatedjuice by removingpH7.0; frozen200G_PER_L also loses the TOGO volume unit. Source TOGO M4 explicitly identifies filtered tomato juice atpH7.0, separate from final medium pH6.0. Preserve a distinct preparation identity and broad relation to filtered tomato juice. Titrant and amount are unspecified; no component or exact equivalence with untreated juice is asserted. Current JCM11 is unavailable, so TOGO is source database evidence, not newly inspected JCM corroboration. MIM#1164 corrected the proposed native grade to NARROW_MATCH; the pinned producer must emit broadMatch to MICRO:0000556 while retaining the exact registry identity.",
