            "disposition": "new_distinct_ingredient_proposal",
            "reasoning": "Original ATCC929 defines Phenol Red0.5% from0.5g phenol red,1mL6NNaOH and99mL deionized water. The receiving recipe adds0.25mL. This recovered preparation contains alkalinizing reagent and cannot be represented as dry phenol red or assumed identical to the historical Flow stock. Frozen0.25G_PER_L is a unit error. Original ATCC929 enumerates0.5g phenol red,1mL6NNaOH and99mL DIwater, and a0.25mL medium dose. Units denote amounts in the listed100mL liquid-input preparation, not a measured final-volume assertion. This source-specific alkaline indicator is distinct from Flow0.5% phenol-red products whose formulation is unavailable. Do not infer the final dye protonation state or an exact free-acid composition of the resulting alkaline solution. Context-only source labels are retained as non-resolving REJECTED_LABEL; RAW_TEXT source annotations alone do not enforce that scope.",
