            "disposition": "new_distinct_ingredient_proposal",
            "reasoning": "TOGO M2696 identifies Union Carbide SAG-471 antifoam without a dose. The manufacturer-successor Momentive describes SAG 471 as an antifoam compound or concentrate for aqueous and non-aqueous systems. This establishes a product boundary, not an exact identity with pure polydimethylsiloxane or an inferred dosage. Current specifications do not establish the historical Union Carbide formulation. TOGO M2696 explicitly names historical Union Carbide SAG-471. This is a source-qualified commercial antifoam identity with unspecified composition and dose. The current Momentive SAG471 technical sheet corroborates the product-name family, but no identity with the modern formulation, no pure-PDMS identity, component proportion, lot or recipe dose is asserted. Unknown historical formulation details do not prevent preserving the established named product as an undefined mixture.",
            "applicability": "Individually reviewed source case 114: 'Antifoam (Union Carbide Corp., SAG-471)'; all 1 original occurrence IDs and full frozen recipe contexts are retained in RS-114-FROZEN. Primary references are scoped to those exact recipes or explicitly identified chemical/product candidates; no identity or concentration is transferred to a different preparation. This review preserves every inherited source/native hold and does not approve roles or release.",
