            "reasoning": "The admitted full J451 recipe adds 30 ml of 84 g/L NaHCO3 solution, autoclaved under CO2, after the basal recipe is sterilized and cooled under N2/CO2. This supports a concentration-defined prepared bicarbonate stock and the existing local stock record as a source-label candidate, not neat CHEBI:32139 identity. The live JCM451 response is Nothing found and supplies no formulation evidence; the admitted 2026-11-05 MediaDive body supplies the actual recipe claim. Current owner aliases include the bare fragment (5% w/v solution), which denotes 50 g/L if applied to this bicarbonate stock and therefore cannot name an 84 g/L stock, and the non-name (after autoclaving). Native synonym_policy already excludes both bare parentheticals despite RAW_TEXT typing; the proposal is optional explicit provenance typing and does not repair an active resolver/export leak.",
