            "reasoning": "DSMZ1433 specifies 5 g Sigmacell alpha Type 50 (Sigma S5504). The current official S5504 page identifies Sigmacell Cellulose, Type 50, 50 micrometres, CAS 9004-34-6, and separately lists alpha-cellulose C6429 as another product. The catalog code therefore supports this specific cellulose product, while the recipe word alpha is retained as source wording rather than used to assert a polymorph, alpha-cellulose grade or different catalog identity. The existing UNMAPPED_0520 is the corresponding source-label placeholder; bulk cellulose equivalence would lose the Type50 physical product detail. Completeness reassessment: Original DSMZ1433 explicitly specifies Sigma S5504. The current official S5504 specification identifies Sigmacell cellulose Type50, nominal particle size50 micrometres. Retain the original alpha wording as a source label, but do not equate this product to the separately listed alpha-cellulose product C6429 or assign the supplier web page disaccharide SMILES to the polymer. The registry identifies the source-specific cellulose preparation, not generic cellulose as an exact identity. An isolated guarded existing-owner promotion now supplies the exact registry identity and supported material scope.",
            "applicability": "Applies only to this exact source profile and source_case_id, preserving its raw label and frozen count definition. All admitted recipe contexts and embedded downstream holds are bound by the case evidence. Listed owner records are inspected current candidates; a candidate is approved only to the narrow scope expressly stated in reasoning. Registry correspondence does not approve external chemistry, whole owner records, biological claims or complete SSSOM payloads.",
