            "occurrence_ids": [],
            "disposition": "supplied_form_correction",
            "reasoning": "Both DSMZ1493 and1685 specify 0.440 g Na2SeO4 x 10 H2O in the shared one-litre trace solution, after dissolving nitrilotriacetic acid and adjusting pH. The supplied form is explicitly sodium selenate decahydrate. Current Na2seo4.yaml denotes CHEBI:77775, whose official structure and formula 2Na.O4Se are anhydrous; it already rejects the decahydrate alias. The hydrate must remain distinct. Its formula is source supported, but assigning the anhydrous identifier to it would erase ten waters. Completeness reassessment: Original DSMZ1493/1685 explicitly use Na2SeO4·10H2O. Current official Thermo specification identifies CAS10102-23-5 and H20Na2O14Se; original crystallography DOI10.1107/S1600536814011799 confirms the decahydrate. Current OLS exact-name query returned no term; CHEBI77775 has anhydrous formula2Na.O4Se/CAS13410-01-0 and is only a broader form anchor. A complete isolated new-owner proposal is supplied. CoordinatorMIM1164 identified the initialdraftBROAD_MATCH grade wouldprojectcloseMatch. Artifactv2 nowusesNARROW_MATCH for intendedskos:broadMatch; the exactspecificCASidentityandsoluteparentareunchanged. Actualpinnedproducerprojectionisrequiredandownedbycoordinator.",
