            },
            "occurrence_ids": [],
            "disposition": "broad_parent_relation_only",
            "reasoning": "The nine admitted rows in media 1191, 1279, 1600 and 1793 consistently specify demineralized water, including one sterile addition in 1600. Original DSMZ recipes retain demineralized water (Aqua dem. in 1279). The current Distilled_Water owner already marks this label REJECTED_LABEL: a common H2O molecular parent does not establish the same water treatment or purity preparation. This case is a preparation-qualified solvent; neither distilled nor tap water is asserted as its exact identity. Completeness reassessment: The source grade demineralized water is explicitly named in all nine admitted ingredient1448 rows across DSMZ1191,1279,1600 and1793, including the source abbreviations H2O demin. and Aqua dem. It is represented as a distinct preparation-qualified solvent, with CHEBI15377 water as a broader molecular parent only. No ion-removal method, conductivity, resistivity, reagent standard, quantitative purity or universal sterility is asserted. The one sterile addition in DSMZ1600 retains that operational qualifier in its recipe; this owner does not globally equate sterile water, distilled water or tap water. The exact-name OLS search found TransformON c_ROHSUO, but TFO is outside the maintained OntologySourceEnum and its conductivity scope is not specified by these sources; the candidate is preserved as context rather than silently adopted or reported absent. A distinct guarded registry proposal supplies the supported water-grade identity; unspecified numerical purity is not an integration blocker.",
            "applicability": "Applies only to this exact source profile and source_case_id, preserving its raw label and frozen count definition. All admitted recipe contexts and embedded downstream holds are bound by the case evidence. Listed owner records are inspected current candidates; a candidate is approved only to the narrow scope expressly stated in reasoning. Registry correspondence does not approve external chemistry, whole owner records, biological claims or complete SSSOM payloads.",
