            "reasoning": "TOGO M1094/JCM1030 explicitly states chromium potassium double sulfate with twelve waters. The dot variant retains the same Cr:K:sulfate:water 1:1:2:12 ratio as the supplier chrome-alum CAS7788-99-0 and existing owner. It can share the alias proposal with the spaced MediaDive spelling. Exact active MeSHM0314280 now provides dodecahydrate identity; preserve ownCAS7788-99-0 as a chemical property and retire the incomplete prior CHEBI53471 CLOSE rationale.",
            "applicability": "All 1 original occurrences were reviewed in their complete frozen recipe contexts. Evidence applies to the exact preserved source label 'CrK(SO4)2·12H2O'; source component, stock, salt, hydration and charge scopes are interpreted only as stated in the case reasoning. No inherited hold or downstream identity authorization is removed. Source-unit discrepancy: TOGO M1094 trace solution gives CrK(SO4)2·12H2O as0.5mg, while the frozen flattened occurrence records0.5G_PER_L. This identity/alias proposal approves neither that normalization nor any receiving-medium concentration. Positive source support excludes the failed JCM1033 response. Exact form mapping does not authorize any source quantity normalization.",
