      "cases": [
        {
          "actual_case_owner_slot": "worker-02",
          "actual_decision_core": {
            "destination": "reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-02/seven-preparation-types-v1/selected-v3/decisions.json",
            "source": "/Users/marcin/Documents/VIMSS/ontology/Mechs/MediaIngredientMech/.temp/all-unmatched-20261107/integration/final-campaign-planning-v1/observed-inputs-v1/snapshot/w02/reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-02/seven-preparation-types-v1/selected-v3/decisions.json",
            "sha256": "9ff9a43085636f5d3a812029beb0d2065eed443695ac8e0ff9e14d1e6e9c91d2",
            "size": 786343
          },
          "selector": "/decisions/179",
          "case_input_sha256": "74678ee9a1662a2a5bc00b8ed03fc1467adbec1dbee1a16192a726cf590a8d6d",
          "case_object_sha256": "49884f09320402f6340ac1830f8f1568d5b4005ad4b2842f91cd346fecf62928",
          "case": {
            "case_id": "KG_CASE:e4c29602025f8838c699c48836a45f5567ad8994a4ec756fed88da2647542689",
            "case_input_sha256": "74678ee9a1662a2a5bc00b8ed03fc1467adbec1dbee1a16192a726cf590a8d6d",
            "source": {
              "source": "metatraits",
              "source_case_id": "kgmicrobe.compound:o_carbamyl_d_serine",
              "source_label": "O-carbamyl-D-serine",
              "raw_source_label": ""
            },
            "occurrence_ids": [],
            "disposition": "supplied_form_correction",
            "reasoning": "The frozen graph name explicitly specifies O-carbamyl-D-serine. Primary NLM shows that current descriptor C000366 has broader preferred concept M0040465 with distinct narrower D concept M0040464 and L concept M0307419; OLS exports both as related synonyms, so a synonym hit does not justify the existing descriptor-level exact identity. PubChem122679 independently identifies the (2R)/D compound as CAS3819-76-9, and the Funakoshi/Institute of Microbial Chemistry20324 product confirms the same CAS/name. The original1968 paper characterizes O-carbamyl-D-serine and D-serine produced by hydrolysis. The proposal uses exact NLM concept mesh:M0040464 for the named D identity, replacing the broader descriptor. The production local adapter resolves that canonical concept label, and the schema admits the mesh prefix; the OLS descriptor-only search did not establish absence or ineligibility of this exact target. No production-organism or role claim is inferred for the frozen incident edge.",
