            "reasoning": "MediaDive1000 expressly names MnSO4 xnH2O and supplies no fixed-hydrate identifiers. The all-owner lookup found fixed one/two/four/five/six/seven-water records and anhydrous MnSO4, but no matching variable-hydrate owner. Variable hydration is the supported substance scope, not a missing fact requiring a guessed n. Continuation A proposes the shared variable-hydrate identity supported by Sigma229784 and the hydration-unspecified CAS15244-36-7; this case links that proposal without inventing a fixed molecular weight or structure.",
            "applicability": "Issue1201 continuation of this exact frozen source case. MediaDive1000 expressly names MnSO4 xnH2O and supplies no fixed-hydrate identifiers. The all-owner lookup found fixed one/two/four/five/six/seven-water records and anhydrous MnSO4, but no matching variable-hydrate owner. Variable hydration is the supported substance scope, not a missing fact requiring a guessed n. Continuation A proposes the shared variable-hydrate identity supported by Sigma229784 and the hydration-unspecified CAS15244-36-7; this case links that proposal without inventing a fixed molecular weight or structure. Helper/incident-edge count definitions, original source ID and raw label are unchanged. Every inherited nonpositive row decision, source placeholder and downstream hold remains in force. Scope-specific proposals do not approve generic labels globally or release complete owner/export payloads.",
