            "applicability": "All original frozen occurrence IDs and full recipe contexts are preserved. JCM673 explicitly specifies Fe2(SO4)3·xH2O. Variable x and n both leave water stoichiometry unspecified and match the existing variable-ferric-sulfate-hydrate identity now proposed as cas:15244-10-7. The broad CHEBI53438 parent remains asymmetric and does not identify a fixed hydrate. Wako primary sources support own CAS15244-10-7 for the variable-n material; CHEBI131387 monohydrate is not exact. The malformed competing UNMAPPED0385 identity under873 is not resolved or merged. Supplier evidence identifies chemical scope only, not historical procurement, assay or receiving-medium quantities. Old failed JCM1250 capture is unsuccessful access, not positive recipe evidence. Every original source/release hold remains.",
