                "assessment": "Promote the variable-n ferric sulfate primary identity to cas:15244-10-7 under MAPPING_SEMANTICS§3: independent Wako product pages explicitly pair that CAS with Fe2(SO4)3·nH2O. Retain CHEBI53438 iron(3+) sulfate as the asymmetric broader grounding (NARROW_MATCH); do not use CHEBI131387 monohydrate as exact, copy anhydrous formula weight, select n, or assert historical lot procurement. The old no-own-CAS rationale is superseded, with its full original preserved in predecessor evidence/history. JCM413→369 and603→592 are available:369 separately autoclaves0.5% variable-ferric-sulfate solution in0.1N H2SO4 (percent basis unspecified);592 includes0.01g variable ferric sulfate in SolutionA alongside distinct ferrous sulfate and ferric citrate. Failed JCM1250 Nothing-found retrieval is not positive source proof; source-specific TOGO evidence is separately bound. The competing UNMAPPED0385 owner and issue873 remain unresolved; no winner or merge is selected."
