            "reasoning": "Paraamino specifies the amino group para to the benzoic-acid carboxyl group, matching CHEBI30753 4-aminobenzoic acid. Both TOGO3160/3161 frozen vitamin contexts preserve this unqualified acid; no salt, stock or other isomer qualifier is present. Additional inherited-owner context only: the historical p-aminobenzoic acid(0.3μg/μL) alias is a preparation corroborated by NBRC1604/TOGO M3052, now proposed separately. This does not say the two frozen Paraamino benzoic acid occurrences in M3160/M3161 use that stock.",
            "applicability": "Case index 69: all 2 original occurrences and complete frozen recipe snapshots were read. Paraamino specifies the amino group para to the benzoic-acid carboxyl group, matching CHEBI30753 4-aminobenzoic acid. Both TOGO3160/3161 frozen vitamin contexts preserve this unqualified acid; no salt, stock or other isomer qualifier is present. Evidence from another recipe or manufacturer is used only for the stated chemical/form comparison, never to replace missing source recipe context. All frozen downstream/native holds remain in force.",
