            "disposition": "existing_identity_or_alias",
            "reasoning": "The three frozen occurrences explicitly specify three sodium ions. Live CHEBI:63125 defines the trisodium salt, distinct from disodium CHEBI:64734/64758. The owner is correctly trisodium but its active 'EDTA di sodium salt' synonym is chemically wrong. Add the explicit 3Na spelling and retain the wrong disodium string only as rejected provenance; no interpretation of case125 is imported here. Original NBRC387/900/391 all corroborate3Na-EDTA; NBRC387 specifies200mg in a vitamin stock, not the frozen200g/L flattened component.",
            "applicability": "Applies only to frozen case CM_NAME:02591f4a5364db919b1a8890e8f6800a87eea943fff102ed0405d0de9b069fa5, source culturemech, identifier 3Na-EDTA; every listed recipe context and exact raw/processed label remains bound by case_input_sha256. Matching lexical labels do not extend source identity to unrelated cases. All inherited downstream and complete-payload publication holds remain in force.",
