            "disposition": "new_distinct_ingredient_proposal",
            "reasoning": "Primary Sitrin et al.1985 isolated aridicins A/B/C separately by preparative HPLC and characterized B (Table1 empirical formula C82H84N8O30Cl4). Chung et al.1986 printed652 explicitly states aridicin was renamed ardacin, and Figure1 distinguishes the B factor. The existing kgmicrobe.compound:ardacin_b owner can therefore represent this distinct factor with an asymmetric glycopeptide-class parent CHEBI:24396. This is not an exact or broader relation to generic NCIT:C169786 or CHEBI:753252 ardacin complex; those terms lack an independently inspected factor-B definition. No supplier, pure preparation, CAS or reconstructed stereostructure is invented.",
