            "disposition": "stock_product_mixture_context",
            "reasoning": "NBRC 355 directs adding HCl to warmed milk to coagulate it, centrifuging, and using the supernatant as cheese whey. The source-defined output can be represented without a quantified yield. Starting milk and HCl are processing inputs; precipitated milk proteins are removed, and their masses or final retained fractions are not asserted as has-part components. Applies only to CultureMech 015901/nbrc.medium 355 in case 23. DSMZ 775 and JCM 162 name cheese whey as the liquid substrate without the NBRC 355 acid-coagulation preparation. This is the source-stated cheese-whey material class, with unspecified production process and composition, not purified lactose, whole milk or a 1 g/L chemical. The six non-NBRC 355 occurrences are covered; primary 1 L/1000 ml quantities and malformed frozen G_PER_L or PERCENT_V_V values remain distinct evidence.",
            "applicability": "Applies only to culturemech Cheese whey (raw label 'Cheese whey'). All 7 occurrence components and full frozen recipe snapshots were read, including preparation and nested solutions: CultureMech:006432 ingredients/9, CultureMech:008087 ingredients/6, CultureMech:011037 composition/9, CultureMech:012893 composition/9, CultureMech:002521 ingredients/9, CultureMech:001909 ingredients/9, CultureMech:015901 ingredients/9.",
