            "reasoning": "NBRC 1221 and NBRC 1474 each name a 1 M HEPES-KOH stock and add 20 ml. The reported pH values 7.14 and 9.0 belong to the receiving media. Stock pH, neutralization ratio and solvent are unreported. These omissions prove neither equality nor difference. The two accessions support the same bounded nominal preparation description; whether one shared nominal owner or a more specific source-supported representation should be installed remains a coordinator decision under #1237. This identifier is retained only as a conditional historical proposal handle, not a selected stable owner. Do not install both candidates as proven distinct substances. Preserve both source and occurrence routes, all component uncertainty and all inherited holds. The two sources name a whole 1 M HEPES-KOH stock without enumerating material constituents. NEW-02 withdraws the inferred HEPES moiety and potassium-species material partonomy while preserving the useful nominal preparation description.",
