            "reasoning": "JCM1331 titanium-citrate stock and JCM1492 iron stock explicitly use sodium citrate·2H2O. The solid input is sodium citrate dihydrate CHEBI32142, not the resulting titanium/iron solution. Add the exact spelling only; source amount/final-volume discrepancies belong to recipe correction, not identity. This is a documented conventional substance name: independent Sigma W302600 and Thermo S279 specifications explicitly equate sodium citrate dihydrate with trisodium citrate dihydrate, CAS6132-04-3, matching CHEBI32142. This nomenclature evidence supports the name-to-substance interpretation only; it does not assert that JCM bought either supplier product. Bare sodium NTA/malate lacks an equivalently specific hydrate-qualified naming witness in these cases.",
            "applicability": "Applies to exact raw source label 'Sodium citrate·2H2O' and all 2 frozen occurrence objects, each verified against its complete recipe snapshot hash. JCM1331 titanium-citrate stock and JCM1492 iron stock explicitly use sodium citrate·2H2O. The solid input is sodium citrate dihydrate CHEBI32142, not the resulting titanium/iron solution. Add the exact spelling only; source amount/final-volume discrepancies belong to recipe correction, not identity. This is a documented conventional substance name: independent Sigma W302600 and Thermo S279 specifications explicitly equate sodium citrate dihydrate with trisodium citrate dihydrate, CAS6132-04-3, matching CHEBI32142. This nomenclature evidence supports the name-to-substance interpretation only; it does not assert that JCM bought either supplier product. Bare sodium NTA/malate lacks an equivalently specific hydrate-qualified naming witness in these cases.",
