            "disposition": "new_distinct_ingredient_proposal",
            "reasoning": "The17 occurrences were split by their actual cited papers and each original was pursued. Schaechter1958 Table1 p594 explicitly gives Na(NH4)HPO4·4H2O1.74g/L in salt solution(c), used by all nine frozen Schaechter rows; these resolve to CAS7783-13-3, independently confirmed by official supplier formula evidence. Follonier2011 distinguishes E2 flask medium from its separate bioreactor recipe; the latter's literal NaNH4PO4·4H2O omits the acidH and cannot settle the three E2 flask records. Durner fulltext returned403. Four Hassan and oneTseng occurrence remain unconfirmed after exact publisher/PMC fulltext attempts. The family ledger binds all17 individually; no class-wide microcosmic-salt assumption is made.",
