            "disposition": "stock_product_mixture_context",
            "reasoning": "The exact MediaDive1754 source supplies1000mL and references JCM60/ISP-5, whose official formulation is captured. Existing UNMAPPED_0122 instead originated from a generic synonym extracted from Agar.yaml; it has no source1754/JCM60 provenance, component ratios, supplier or formulation version. Its later Edison history quotes ISP medium5 only as a suggested name, not a primary formulation-equivalence finding. Source1754 is therefore a verified JCM60 medium reference, while equivalence of the complete generic owner to this exact recipe remains unproved. Propose a narrow source-provenance note so the supported recipe and remaining identity boundary are durable.",
            "applicability": "Only source ingredient1754 and its1000mL quantity are linked to JCM60. That recipe uses L-asparagine1g, glycerol10g, K2HPO4 1g, agar15g and1mL trace stock per1L distilled water, pH7.4; trace stock has0.1g each FeSO4.7H2O, MnCl2.4H2O and ZnSO4.7H2O per100mL. These are recipe-specific facts, not asserted composition of every material called glycerol-asparagine agar.",
