            "disposition": "stock_product_mixture_context",
            "reasoning": "Recovered TOGO M2809 comments explicitly define the LS4D vitamin preparation in distilled water and identify DL-pantothenic acid as calcium salt, while the structured row drops that qualifier. The actual cited CultureBotHT Mixes rows 88–98 independently confirm the existing owner's cyanocobalamin and calcium-pantothenate assertions. A generic TOGO B12 label does not invalidate that more specific primary source. Propose existing-owner notes/history enrichment with both source formulations and preparation limits; preserve components and avoid a potentially duplicate registry owner.",
            "applicability": "Exact frozen LS4D Thauers vitamins case, all source context retained; actual existing owner and its original primary sheet inspected. Recovered TOGO M2809 comments explicitly define the LS4D vitamin preparation in distilled water and identify DL-pantothenic acid as calcium salt, while the structured row drops that qualifier. The actual cited CultureBotHT Mixes rows 88–98 independently confirm the existing owner's cyanocobalamin and calcium-pantothenate assertions. A generic TOGO B12 label does not invalidate that more specific primary source. Propose existing-owner notes/history enrichment with both source formulations and preparation limits; preserve components and avoid a potentially duplicate registry owner.",
