            "disposition": "stock_product_mixture_context",
            "reasoning": "Split the six occurrences by formula. NBRC 1050/1086/1274/925 match the existing proposed NBRC 1356 common nine-vitamin recipe and join its successor; NBRC 1226(B12 5 mg, lipoic5 mg, pABA 1 mg) and NBRC 903(B12 0.1 mg, lipoic5 mg, pABA 5 mg) each receive a separate stock proposal. The generic calcium-pantothenate wording is not changed to a D-specific form.\n\nCurrent issue1237 supersession: Issue1237 current comparator supersession: this existing CultureBotHT owner correction is causally required by the NBRC903 comparison in W08 case CM_NAME:d57e91ffaea6f0ab6ff0f3d6f0b04c26356c832e85dd83e9e2319874fda43506, triggered only by CM_OCC:a181b24b7eb91c50c771bd1c1fc3012fd0cf28f45b49f2750c3d43bda9cdd531 (CultureMech:007503, frozen NBRC_904.yaml ingredient9). None of the six NBRC case observations is asserted to be a CB occurrence; zero CB campaign occurrences are claimed. The original NBRC903 new-owner proposal and its null beforeimage remain immutable reconciliation input. JCM197/NBRC837/NBRC903 support one common nominal ten-vitamin recipe with 1L distilled-water input batch and source-specific preparation; generic B12 and unspecified calcium-pantothenate stereochemistry remain explicit. Exact association with this CB concentration/X100 definition is unproven. The W06 JCM197 and W08 NBRC903 source-number candidates require central duplicate reconciliation, not installation as two owners or a new human-permission requirement. No W06 case ownership, nominal identifier mint, dose scaling, global exact alias, maintained application or role/export approval is introduced.\n\nCurrent SCI-TENVIT-003 dependency: SCI-TENVIT-003 dependent comparator correction, triggered by the existing NBRC903 occurrence CM_OCC:a181b24b7eb91c50c771bd1c1fc3012fd0cf28f45b49f2750c3d43bda9cdd531 in W08 case CM_NAME:d57e91ffaea6f0ab6ff0f3d6f0b04c26356c832e85dd83e9e2319874fda43506. The separately reviewed ten-vitamin sources and McCas protocol support a common nominal laboratory recipe; generic CultureBot Wolfe also overlaps nominally. Final occurrence association and cross-owner routing remain pending the bounded W04/coordinator decision. Neither Mc nor CB is declared the exclusive owner, and no duplicate nominal owner, merge, source-number identity or inherited owner/role/export approval is introduced. This dependency claims zero Mc campaign occurrences; the authentic Mc source statistics remain22. The other five occurrences in the mixed W08 case and the external eight-case/71CM/84KG/six-exclusion envelope remain unchanged.",
            "applicability": "Issue1201 reassessment of this exact frozen case, all 6 exposed occurrences and complete source contexts. Split the six occurrences by formula. NBRC 1050/1086/1274/925 match the existing proposed NBRC 1356 common nine-vitamin recipe and join its successor; NBRC 1226(B12 5 mg, lipoic5 mg, pABA 1 mg) and NBRC 903(B12 0.1 mg, lipoic5 mg, pABA 5 mg) each receive a separate stock proposal. The generic calcium-pantothenate wording is not changed to a D-specific form.\n\nNBRC903 alone triggers the existing-owner comparator correction; common-nine and NBRC1226 branches remain exact. This is not a mapping of any occurrence to the CB stock.\n\nOnly NBRC903 triggers the Mc comparator correction. The supported nominal recipe comparison is distinct from pending W04 cross-owner association. No actual occurrence is newly mapped to Mc; original source labels, doses, six-occurrence partition and exclusions remain.",
